<title>UK: Cadbury up on continued bid speculation.</title>
<headline>Cadbury up on continued bid speculation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Cadbury Schweppes Plc were up 10p to 495 on renewed bid speculation, with Unilever Plc seen as a possible predator, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a typical Friday story. Unilever has long been tipped as having its eye on Cadbury,&quot; the head of trading at a large investment bank said.</p>
<p>&quot;Now that Unilever has said it will get rid of its chemicals business, people think it will use the cash to go on the acquisition trail.&quot;</p>
<p>On February 11, the Anglo-Dutch consumer products giant said it planned to sell its speciality chemical business, which had turnover of three billion stg in 1996.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
